{"id": "EUVD-2026-107375", "enisaUuid": "290e35fa-4e21-36b0-9215-407e531d0802", "description": "A vulnerability in the Snort 3 Visual Basic for Applications (VBA) Decompression Engine of multiple Cisco products could allow an unauthenticated, remote attacker to cause the Snort 3 Detection Engine to restart unexpectedly, resulting in a denial of service (DoS) condition.&nbsp;&nbsp;\r\n\r\nThis vulnerability is due to improper range checking when Snort 3 decompresses VBA data, which is user controlled. An attacker could exploit this vulnerability by sending crafted VBA data to the Snort 3 Detection Engine of a targeted device. A successful exploit could allow the attacker to cause an overflow of stack data, which could result in a DoS condition.", "datePublished": "2026-10-21T16:12:38", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-22T19:11:10", "baseScore": 5.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:C/C:N/I:N/A:L", "references": ["https://sec.cloudapps.cisco.com/security/center/content/CiscoSecurityAdvisory/cisco-sa-snort3-vba-bufdos-jAuFdvn9"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-20218", "GHSA-vvhg-cxrm-qp98"], "assigner": "cisco", "epss": 0.42, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0237e1af-9898-36b9-a4d7-3af2d1e7ce17", "product": {"name": "Cisco Open Source Snort3", "vendor": {"name": "Cisco"}}, "product_version": "3.1.4.0"}, {"id": "0244f3b6-9ee8-32da-bb37-e08b74ab7ce6", "product": {"name": "Cisco Open Source Snort3", "vendor": {"name": "Cisco"}}, "product_version": "3.1.32.0"}, {"id": "03786db2-aa4f-3125-891d-aa40de69b18f", "product": {"name": "Cisco UTD SNORT IPS Engine Software", "vendor": {"name": "Cisco"}}, "product_version": "17.12.7b"}, {"id": "03b1f1ad-c71d-346a-a6f5-784a8b2282d2", "product": {"name": "Cisco Secure Firewall Threat Defense (FTD) Software", "vendor": {"name": "Cisco"}}, "product_version": "7.4.4"}, {"id": "04b458e7-a28e-3cb5-9716-3838f195b092", "product": {"name": "Cisco Secure Firewall Threat Defense (FTD) Software", "vendor": {"name": "Cisco"}},